Body:
You can define the same upstream model more than once by giving each entry a different key while setting the same `id` on both entries. The map key is the model ID OpenCode exposes in the picker; `id` is the model ID sent to the provider API.

For example:

```jsonc
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "myprovider": {
      "models": {
        "my-model-32k": {
          "id": "actual-upstream-model-id",
          "name": "My Model (32k)",
          "limit": {
            "context": 32768,
            "output": 8192
          }
        },
        "my-model-128k": {
          "id": "actual-upstream-model-id",
          "name": "My Model (128k)",
          "limit": {
            "context": 131072,
            "output": 8192
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

You can then select `myprovider/my-model-32k` or `myprovider/my-model-128k`. Both call `actual-upstream-model-id`, but OpenCode treats them as separate configured models with separate limits.

The OpenCode 1.x provider configuration and model limit fields are documented here: https://opencode.ai/docs/providers/#custom-provider
